var e={"kaoyan2-2025-real":{subtitle:`2025 年 · 站内收录`,minutes:180,words:4200,tags:[`真题`,`考研英语二`],summary:`2025 年考研英语（二）真题站内收录：完形填空、四篇阅读理解、新题型、段落翻译与两篇写作全部题面、选项与参考答案，解析基于公开解析资料与原文定位整理；答案为公开渠道汇总的非官方参考答案。`,parts:[{id:`cloze`,kind:`cloze`,title:`Section I  Use of English`,instructions:`Directions: Read the following text. Choose the best word(s) for each numbered blank and mark A, B, C or D on the ANSWER SHEET. (10 points)`,minutes:20,questions:[{id:`kaoyan2-2025-real-c1`,number:1,type:`single`,stem:`Psychologists have been interested in this ___1___ for decades, not least because people's widespread ___2___ to ask for help has led to some high-profile failures.`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`illusion`},{key:`B`,text:`discussion`},{key:`C`,text:`tradition`},{key:`D`,text:`question`}],answer:`D`,explanation:`答案 D。线索：this 回指 "求助难" 这个值得研究的议题线索就在前一句 There are many understandable reasons why you might find it difficult to ask for help when you need it.:作者把 "开口求助难" 当成一个值得心理学家研究几十年的现象/问题。指向答案应具备 "可供长期研究的议题/问题" 这一语义特征。`,score:.5},{id:`kaoyan2-2025-real-c2`,number:2,type:`single`,stem:`Psychologists have been interested in this ___1___ for decades, not least because people's widespread ___2___ to ask for help has led to some high-profile failures.`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`reluctance`},{key:`B`,text:`ambition`},{key:`C`,text:`tendency`},{key:`D`,text:`enthusiasm`}],answer:`A`,explanation:`答案 A。线索：求助难、且导致 high-profile failures,方向负面前句 There are many understandable reasons why you might find it difficult to ask for help 已经定性 "难以求助";本句又说 people's widespread __(2)__ to ask for help has led to some high-profile failures,明确这种倾向引发了重大失败。线索指向 "不愿/抗拒求助" 这一负面倾向。`,score:.5},{id:`kaoyan2-2025-real-c3`,number:3,type:`single`,stem:`Asking for help takes ___3___.`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`attention`},{key:`B`,text:`talent`},{key:`C`,text:`courage`},{key:`D`,text:`patience`}],answer:`C`,explanation:`答案 C。线索：下文讲暴露弱点、怕显得无能话题句 Asking for help takes __(3)__. 之后紧跟 It involves communicating a need on your part—there's something you can't do. 和 you're broadcasting your own weaknesses, which can be __(5)__.——求助意味着暴露弱点、承认自己做不到,这是需要克服心理障碍才能做到的事。线索指向 "勇气" 这一品质。`,score:.5},{id:`kaoyan2-2025-real-c4`,number:4,type:`single`,stem:`It involves communicating a need on your part-there's something you can't do. ___4___, you're broadcasting your own weaknesses, which can be ___5___.`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`At any time`},{key:`B`,text:`In other words`},{key:`C`,text:`By all means`},{key:`D`,text:`On the contrary`}],answer:`B`,explanation:`答案 B。线索：前后两句是同义改写关系前句 It involves communicating a need on your part—there's something you can't do. 说求助等于承认自己有做不到的事;本句 __(4)__ you're broadcasting your own weaknesses 进一步把 "承认做不到" 换成 "广而告之自己的弱点"——同一事实换种说法。`,score:.5},{id:`kaoyan2-2025-real-c5`,number:5,type:`single`,stem:`It involves communicating a need on your part-there's something you can't do. ___4___, you're broadcasting your own weaknesses, which can be ___5___.`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`unrealistic`},{key:`B`,text:`deceptive`},{key:`C`,text:`tiresome`},{key:`D`,text:`uncomfortable`}],answer:`D`,explanation:`答案 D。线索：暴露弱点带来心理不适 you're broadcasting your own weaknesses, which can be __(5)__. 中 which 指 "广播自己的弱点",后文 You might worry about coming across as incompetent. 进一步描述这种心理负担。线索指向 "令人不舒服"。`,score:.5},{id:`kaoyan2-2025-real-c6`,number:6,type:`single`,stem:`You might have ___6___ about losing control of whatever it is you're asking for help with, ___7___ someone starts to help, perhaps they'd take over, or get credit for your earlier efforts.`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`doubts`},{key:`B`,text:`concerns`},{key:`C`,text:`suggestions`},{key:`D`,text:`secrets`}],answer:`B`,explanation:`答案 B。线索：about 后接 "失去控制" 是负面顾虑 You might have __(6)__ about losing control of whatever it is you're asking for help with. 后接 losing control 这种典型负面情境;前句 You might worry about coming across as incompetent. 已经定调为 "worry" 一类的担忧。线索指向 "担忧、顾虑" 这种情绪名词。`,score:.5},{id:`kaoyan2-2025-real-c7`,number:7,type:`single`,stem:`You might have ___6___ about losing control of whatever it is you're asking for help with, ___7___ someone starts to help, perhaps they'd take over, or get credit for your earlier efforts.`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`Once`},{key:`B`,text:`Unless`},{key:`C`,text:`Although`},{key:`D`,text:`Before`}],answer:`A`,explanation:`答案 A。线索：他人开始帮忙是 "被接管/抢功" 的前提 __(7)__ someone starts to help, perhaps they'll take over, or get credit for your earlier efforts. 显示前分句是触发条件,后分句是可能的结果。"一旦有人开始帮忙" 才会发生 "接管" 或 "抢功"。`,score:.5},{id:`kaoyan2-2025-real-c8`,number:8,type:`single`,stem:`Yet another ___8___ that you might be worried about is being a nuisance or ___9___ the person you go to for help.`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`theory`},{key:`B`,text:`choice`},{key:`C`,text:`factor`},{key:`D`,text:`context`}],answer:`C`,explanation:`答案 C。线索：前文列举的都是 "让你担心的顾虑因素" 前文已列 You might worry about coming across as incompetent.、You might have __(6)__ about losing control、__(7)__ someone starts to help, perhaps they'll take over 等多条,都是 "让你担心而不敢求助的因素"。线索指向 "因素" 这一概括类别。`,score:.5},{id:`kaoyan2-2025-real-c9`,number:9,type:`single`,stem:`Yet another ___8___ that you might be worried about is being a nuisance or ___9___ the person you go to for help.`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`overpraising`},{key:`B`,text:`outperforming`},{key:`C`,text:`reassessing`},{key:`D`,text:`inconveniencing`}],answer:`D`,explanation:`答案 D。线索：前并列项是 "being a nuisance" Yet another __(8)__ that you might be worried about is being a nuisance or __(9)__ the person you go to for help. 中 or 前并列项是 "being a nuisance(成为麻烦/讨厌的人)",or 后必须是相近的负面行为,且能接 the person 作宾语。线索指向 "给别人添麻烦"。`,score:.5},{id:`kaoyan2-2025-real-c10`,number:10,type:`single`,stem:`If you struggle with low self-esteem, you might find it especially difficult to ___10___ for help because you have the added worry of the other person ___11___ your request.`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`reach out`},{key:`B`,text:`settle down`},{key:`C`,text:`turn over`},{key:`D`,text:`look back`}],answer:`A`,explanation:`答案 A。线索：段落主题 "求助难"、空后 for help you might find it especially difficult to __(10)__ for help 主题就是 "开口求助",且空后紧跟 for help。reach out for help 是 "伸手求助" 的固定搭配。本空只需看本句即可定。`,score:.5},{id:`kaoyan2-2025-real-c11`,number:11,type:`single`,stem:`If you struggle with low self-esteem, you might find it especially difficult to ___10___ for help because you have the added worry of the other person ___11___ your request.`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`declining`},{key:`B`,text:`considering`},{key:`C`,text:`criticizing`},{key:`D`,text:`evaluating`}],answer:`A`,explanation:`答案 A。线索：下文 such refusals 直接定性紧随其后的 You might see such refusals as implying something __(12)__ about the status of your relationship with them. 用 such refusals 回指上句的动作。线索锁死答案必须表达 "拒绝"。`,score:.5},{id:`kaoyan2-2025-real-c12`,number:12,type:`single`,stem:`You might see such refusals as implying something ___12___ about the status of your relationship with them.`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`unnecessary`},{key:`B`,text:`negative`},{key:`C`,text:`strange`},{key:`D`,text:`impractical`}],answer:`B`,explanation:`答案 B。线索：整段在讲低自尊的负面解读 If you struggle with low self-esteem, you might find it especially difficult to __(10)__ for help 已定调本段聚焦 "低自尊→负面解读";下一句 To __(13)__ these difficulties, try to remind yourself that everyone needs help sometimes. 把这些解读统称为 difficulties。线索指向 "负面的"。`,score:.5},{id:`kaoyan2-2025-real-c13`,number:13,type:`single`,stem:`To ___13___ these difficulties, try to remind yourself that everyone needs help sometimes.`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`explain`},{key:`B`,text:`identify`},{key:`C`,text:`predict`},{key:`D`,text:`overcome`}],answer:`D`,explanation:`答案 D。线索：后接的是消除负面想法的具体建议 To __(13)__ these difficulties, try to remind yourself that everyone needs help sometimes. 后给出的是 "提醒自己人人都需要帮助" 这样消解 difficulties 的方法,与 "克服" 的目标完全匹配。本空仅看本句即可定。`,score:.5},{id:`kaoyan2-2025-real-c14`,number:14,type:`single`,stem:`And while you might ___14___ coming across as incompetent, there's actually research that shows that advice-seekers are ___15___ as more competent, not less.`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`deny`},{key:`B`,text:`forget`},{key:`C`,text:`miss`},{key:`D`,text:`fear`}],answer:`D`,explanation:`答案 D。线索：while...there's actually research 的让步反转 while you might __(14)__ coming across as incompetent, there's actually research that shows that advice-seekers are __(15)__ as more competent, not less. while 引导让步从句,后半用 actually 强转折,说明前半是 "担心被看作无能"——研究反过来证明并不会。线索指向 "害怕"。`,score:.5},{id:`kaoyan2-2025-real-c15`,number:15,type:`single`,stem:`And while you might ___14___ coming across as incompetent, there's actually research that shows that advice-seekers are ___15___ as more competent, not less.`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`disguised`},{key:`B`,text:`perceived`},{key:`C`,text:`followed`},{key:`D`,text:`introduced`}],answer:`B`,explanation:`答案 B。线索：研究结果是 "别人怎么看求助者" advice-seekers are __(15)__ as more competent, not less 表达的是研究中别人对求助者的看法。线索指向 "被视为"。`,score:.5},{id:`kaoyan2-2025-real-c16`,number:16,type:`single`,stem:`Perhaps most encouraging of all is a paper from 2022 by researchers at Stanford University, in California, that involved a mix of contrived help-seeking interactions and asking people to ___16___ times they'd sought help in the past.`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`recall`},{key:`B`,text:`classify`},{key:`C`,text:`analyse`},{key:`D`,text:`compare`}],answer:`A`,explanation:`答案 A。线索：the past + 让被试做的事 asking people to __(16)__ times they'd sought help in the past 关键在 times they'd sought help in the past——线索指向 "回忆过去经历"。`,score:.5},{id:`kaoyan2-2025-real-c17`,number:17,type:`single`,stem:`The findings showed that help-seekers generally underestimate how ___17___ other people will be to help and how good it'll make the help-giver feel (for most people, having the chance to help someone is highly ___18___).`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`brave`},{key:`B`,text:`disapproving`},{key:`C`,text:`willing`},{key:`D`,text:`hesitant`}],answer:`C`,explanation:`答案 C。线索：研究反转主旨:他人比想象中乐意帮忙 The findings showed that help-seekers generally underestimate how __(17)__ other people will be to help and how good it'll make the help-giver feel 与下文 having the chance to help someone is highly __(18)__ 共同指明研究反转方向:人们 "低估了" 别人 "乐于" 帮忙的程度。线索指向 "愿意的"。`,score:.5},{id:`kaoyan2-2025-real-c18`,number:18,type:`single`,stem:`The findings showed that help-seekers generally underestimate how ___17___ other people will be to help and how good it'll make the help-giver feel (for most people, having the chance to help someone is highly ___18___).`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`relaxing`},{key:`B`,text:`surprising`},{key:`C`,text:`rewarding`},{key:`D`,text:`demanding`}],answer:`C`,explanation:`答案 C。线索：括号外 how good 决定方向前文 how good it'll make the help-giver feel 已经定调帮助他人 "让助人者感觉很好",括号内 having the chance to help someone is highly __(18)__ 是对其进一步具体化。线索指向 "让人有获得感的"。`,score:.5},{id:`kaoyan2-2025-real-c19`,number:19,type:`single`,stem:`So, bear all this in mind the next time you need to ask for help. ___19___, take care over who you ask and when you ask them.`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`Thus`},{key:`B`,text:`Also`},{key:`C`,text:`Finally`},{key:`D`,text:`Instead`}],answer:`B`,explanation:`答案 B。线索：前句给总建议、本句给附加细则前句 So, bear all this in mind the next time you need to ask for help. 是总建议;本句 __(19)__ take care over who you ask and when you ask them. 给出附加的 "选谁问、什么时候问" 细则;后面又接着 And if someone can't help right now, avoid taking it personally. 再加一条,明显是并列累加而非替代或收尾。`,score:.5},{id:`kaoyan2-2025-real-c20`,number:20,type:`single`,stem:`They might just be too ___20___, or they might not feel confident about their ability to help.`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`polite`},{key:`B`,text:`proud`},{key:`C`,text:`busy`},{key:`D`,text:`lazy`}],answer:`C`,explanation:`答案 C。线索：right now + or 平行项的善意基调 And if someone can't help right now, avoid taking it personally. They might just be too __(20)__, or they might not feel confident about their ability to help. 中 right now 暗示时间不凑巧;后并列项 they might not feel confident about their ability to help 是善意中性的原因,作者明显在劝考生不要责怪对方。线索指向 "忙" 这种中性外因。`,score:.5}]},{id:`reading`,kind:`reading`,title:`Section II  Reading Comprehension  Part A`,instructions:`Directions: Read the following four texts. Answer the questions below each text by choosing A, B, C or D. Mark your answers on the ANSWER SHEET. (40 points)`,minutes:70,passages:[{id:`p1`,title:`Text 1`,paragraphs:[{id:`p1-1`,marker:`1`,text:`U.S. customers historically tipped people they assumed were earning most of their income via tips, such as restaurant servers earning less than the minimum wage. In the early 2010s, a wide range of businesses started processing purchases with iPads and other digital payment systems. These systems often prompted customers to tip for services that were not previously tipped.`},{id:`p1-2`,marker:`2`,text:`Today's tip requests are often not connected to the salary and service norms that used to determine when and how people tip. Customers in the past nearly always paid tips after receiving a service, such as at the conclusion of a restaurant meal, after getting a haircut or once a pizza was delivered. That timing could reward high-quality service and give workers an incentive to provide it.`},{id:`p1-3`,marker:`3`,text:`It's becoming more common for tips to be requested beforehand. And new tipping technology may even automatically add tips.`},{id:`p1-4`,marker:`4`,text:`The prevalence of digital payment devices has made it easier to ask customers for a tip. That helps explain why tip requests are creeping into new kinds of services. Customers now routinely see menus of suggested default options-often well above 20% of what they owe. The amounts have risen from 10% or less in the 1950s to 15% around the year 2000 to 20% or higher today. This increase is sometimes called tipflation-the expectation of ever-higher tip amounts.`},{id:`p1-5`,marker:`5`,text:`Tipping has always been a vital source of income for workers in historically tipped services, like restaurants, where the tipped minimum wage can be as low as US$2.13 an hour. Tip creep and tipflation are now further supplementing the income of many low-wage service workers.`},{id:`p1-6`,marker:`6`,text:`Notably, tipping primarily benefits some of these workers, such as waiters, but not others, such as cooks and dishwashers. To ensure that all employees were paid fair wages, some restaurants banned tipping and increased prices, but this movement toward no-tipping services has largely fizzled out.`},{id:`p1-7`,marker:`7`,text:`So, to increase employee wages without raising prices, more employers are succumbing to the temptations of tip creep and tipflation. However, many customers are frustrated because they feel they are being asked for too high of a tip, too often. And, as our research emphasizes, tipping now seems to be more coercive, less generous and often completely disassociated from service quality.`}]},{id:`p2`,title:`Text 2`,paragraphs:[{id:`p2-1`,marker:`1`,text:`When it was established, the National Health Service (NHS) was visionary: offering high-quality, timely care to meet the dominant needs of the population it served. Nearly 75 years on, with the UK facing very different health challenges, it is clear that the model is out of date.`},{id:`p2-2`,marker:`2`,text:`From life expectancy to cancer and infant mortality rates, we are lagging behind many of our peers. With more than 6.8 million on waitlists, healthcare is becoming increasingly inaccessible for those who cannot opt to pay for private treatment; and the cost of providing healthcare is increasingly squeezing out investment in other public services. As demand for healthcare continues to grow, pressures on the workforce-which is already near breaking point-will only become more acute.`},{id:`p2-3`,marker:`3`,text:`Many of the answers to the crisis in health and care are well rehearsed. We need to be much better at reducing and diverting demand on health services, rather than simply managing it. Much more needs to be invested in communities and primary care to reduce our reliance on hospitals. And capacity in social care needs to be greater, to support the growing number of people living with long-term conditions.`},{id:`p2-4`,marker:`4`,text:`Yet despite two decades of strategies and a number of major health reforms, we have failed to make meaningful progress on any of these aims. That is why the Reform think tank is launching a new programme of work entitled “Reimagining health”, supported by ten former health ministers. Together, we are calling for a much more open and honest conversation about the future of health in the UK, and an “urgent rethink” of the hospital-centric model we retain.`},{id:`p2-5`,marker:`5`,text:`This must begin with the question of how we maximise the health of the nation, rather than “fix” the NHS. It is estimated, for example, that healthcare accounts for only about 20% of health outcomes. Much more important are the places we live, work and socialise-yet there is no clear cross-government strategy for improving these social determinants of health. Worse, when policies like the national obesity strategy are scrapped, taxpayers are left with the heavy price tag of treating the illnesses, like diabetes, that result.`},{id:`p2-6`,marker:`6`,text:`Reform wants to ask how power and resources should be distributed in our health system. What health functions should remain at the centre, and what should be given to local leaders, often responsible for services that create health, and with a much better understanding of the needs of their populations?`}]},{id:`p3`,title:`Text 3`,paragraphs:[{id:`p3-1`,marker:`1`,text:`Heat action plans, or HAPs, have been proliferating in India in the past few years. In general, an HAP spells out when and how officials should issue heat warnings and alert hospitals and other institutions. Nagpur's plan, for instance, calls for hospitals to set aside “cold wards” in the summer for treating heatstroke patients, and advises builders to give construction laborers a break from work on very hot days.`},{id:`p3-2`,marker:`2`,text:`But implementation of existing HAPs has been uneven, according to a report from the Center for Policy Research. Many lack adequate funding, it found. And their triggering thresholds often are not customized to the local climate. In some areas, high daytime temperatures alone might serve as an adequate trigger for alerts. But in other places, nighttime temperatures or humidity might be as important a gauge of risk as daytime highs.`},{id:`p3-3`,marker:`3`,text:`Mumbai's April heat stroke deaths highlighted the need for more nuanced and localized warnings, researchers say. That day's high temperature of roughly 36°C was 1°C shy of the heat wave alert threshold for coastal cities set by national meteorological authorities. But the effects of the heat were amplified by humidity-an often neglected factor in heat alert systems-and the lack of shade at the late-morning outdoor ceremony.`},{id:`p3-4`,marker:`4`,text:`To help improve HAPs, urban planner Kotharkar's team is working on a model plan that outlines best practices and could be adapted to local conditions. Among other things, she says, all cities should create a vulnerability map to help focus responses on the populations most at risk.`},{id:`p3-5`,marker:`5`,text:`Such mapping doesn't need to be complex, Kotharkar says. “A useful map can be created by looking at even a few key parameters.” For example, neighborhoods with a large elderly population or informal dwellings that cope poorly with heat could get special warnings or be bolstered with cooling centers. The Nagpur project has already created a risk and vulnerability map, which enabled Kotharkar to tell officials which neighborhoods to focus on in the event of a heat wave this summer.`},{id:`p3-6`,marker:`6`,text:`HAPs shouldn't just include short-term emergency responses, researchers say, but also recommend medium- to long-term measures that could make communities cooler. In Nagpur, for example, Kotharkar's team has been able to advise city officials about where to plant trees to provide shade. HAPs could also guide efforts to retrofit homes or modify building regulations. “Reducing deaths in an emergency is good target to have, but it's the lowest target,” says climate researcher Chandni Singh.`}]},{id:`p4`,title:`Text 4`,paragraphs:[{id:`p4-1`,marker:`1`,text:`Navigating beyond the organised pavements and parks of our urban spaces, desire paths are the unofficial footprints of a community, revealing the unspoken preferences, shared shortcuts and collective choices of humans. Often appearing as trodden dirt tracks through otherwise neat green spaces, these routes of collective disobedience cut corners, bisect lawns and cross hills, representing the natural capability of people (and animals) to go from point A to point B most effectively.`},{id:`p4-2`,marker:`2`,text:`Urban planners interpret desire paths as more than just convenient shortcuts; they offer valuable insights into the dynamics between planning and behaviour. Ohio State University allowed its students to navigate the Oval, a lawn in the centre of campus, freely, then proceeded to pave the desire paths, creating a web of effective routes students had established.`},{id:`p4-3`,marker:`3`,text:`Yet, reluctance persists among other planners to integrate desire paths into formal plans, citing concerns about safety, environmental impact, or primarily, aesthetics. A Reddit webpage devoted to the phenomenon, boasting nearly 50,000 members, showcases images of local desire paths adorned with signs instructing pedestrians to adhere to designated walkways, underscoring the rebellious nature inherent in these human-made tracks. This clash highlights an ongoing struggle between the organic, user-driven evolution of public spaces and the desire for a visually curated and controlled urban environment.`},{id:`p4-4`,marker:`4`,text:`The Wickquasgeck Trail is an example of a historical desire path, created by Native Americans to cross the forests of Manhattan and move between settlements quickly. This trail, when Dutch colonists arrived, was widened and made into one of the main trade roads across the island, known at the time as de Heere Straat, or Gentlemen's Street. Following the British assumption of control in New York, the street was renamed Broadway. Notably, Broadway stands out as one of the few areas in NYC that defies the grid-based system applied to the rest of the city, cutting a diagonal across parts of the city.`},{id:`p4-5`,marker:`5`,text:`In online spaces, desire paths have sparked a fascination that can approach obsession, with the Reddit page serving as a hub. Contributors offer a wide array of stories, from little-known new shortcuts to long-established alternate routes.`},{id:`p4-6`,marker:`6`,text:`Animal desire paths, such as ducks forging trails through frozen ponds or dogs carving direct routes in gardens, highlight the adaptability of these trails in both human and animal experiences. As desire paths criss-cross through both physical and virtual landscapes, they stand as a proof of the collective insistence on forging unconventional routes and embracing the spirit of communal choice.`}]}],questions:[{id:`kaoyan2-2025-real-r21`,number:21,type:`single`,stem:`According to Paragraph 1, the practice of tipping in the U.S ___.`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`was regarded as a sign of generosity`},{key:`B`,text:`was considered essential for waiters`},{key:`C`,text:`was a way of rewarding diligence`},{key:`D`,text:`was optional in most businesses`}],answer:`B`,explanation:`第1段：“U.S. customers historically tipped people they assumed were earning most of their income via tips, such as restaurant servers earning less than the minimum wage.”。该句表述与选项“was considered essential for waiters”一致，故选 B。`,evidence:{paragraphId:`p1-1`,quote:`U.S. customers historically tipped people they assumed were earning most of their income via tips, such as restaurant servers earning less than the minimum wage.`},score:2},{id:`kaoyan2-2025-real-r22`,number:22,type:`single`,stem:`Compared with tips in the past, today's tips ___`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`are paid much less frequently`},{key:`B`,text:`are less often requested in advance`},{key:`C`,text:`have less to do with service quality`},{key:`D`,text:`contribute less to workers' income`}],answer:`C`,explanation:`第2段：“Customers in the past nearly always paid tips after receiving a service, such as at the conclusion of a restaurant meal, after getting a haircut or once a pizza was delivered.”。该句表述与选项“have less to do with service quality”一致，故选 C。`,evidence:{paragraphId:`p1-2`,quote:`Customers in the past nearly always paid tips after receiving a service, such as at the conclusion of a restaurant meal, after getting a haircut or once a pizza was delivered.`},score:2},{id:`kaoyan2-2025-real-r23`,number:23,type:`single`,stem:`Tip requests are creeping into new kinds of services as a result of ___`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`the advancement of technology`},{key:`B`,text:`the desire for income increase`},{key:`C`,text:`the diversification of business`},{key:`D`,text:`the emergence of tipflation`}],answer:`A`,explanation:`第4段：“That helps explain why tip requests are creeping into new kinds of services.”。该句表述与选项“the advancement of technology”一致，故选 A。`,evidence:{paragraphId:`p1-4`,quote:`That helps explain why tip requests are creeping into new kinds of services.`},score:2},{id:`kaoyan2-2025-real-r24`,number:24,type:`single`,stem:`The movement toward no-tipping services was intended to ___`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`promote consumption`},{key:`B`,text:`enrich income sources`},{key:`C`,text:`maintain reasonable prices`},{key:`D`,text:`guarantee income fairness`}],answer:`D`,explanation:`第6段：“To ensure that all employees were paid fair wages, some restaurants banned tipping and increased prices, but this movement toward no-tipping services has largely fizzled out.”。该句表述与选项“guarantee income fairness”一致，故选 D。`,evidence:{paragraphId:`p1-6`,quote:`To ensure that all employees were paid fair wages, some restaurants banned tipping and increased prices, but this movement toward no-tipping services has largely fizzled out.`},score:2},{id:`kaoyan2-2025-real-r25`,number:25,type:`single`,stem:`It can be learned from the last paragraph that tipping ___`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`is becoming a burden for customers`},{key:`B`,text:`helps encourage quality service`},{key:`C`,text:`is vital to business development`},{key:`D`,text:`reflects the need to reduce prices`}],answer:`A`,explanation:`第7段：“However, many customers are frustrated because they feel they are being asked for too high of a tip, too often.”。该句表述与选项“is becoming a burden for customers”一致，故选 A。`,evidence:{paragraphId:`p1-7`,quote:`However, many customers are frustrated because they feel they are being asked for too high of a tip, too often.`},score:2},{id:`kaoyan2-2025-real-r26`,number:26,type:`single`,stem:`According to the first two paragraphs, the NHS ___`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`is troubled by funding deficiencies`},{key:`B`,text:`can hardly satisfy people's needs`},{key:`C`,text:`can barely retain its current employees`},{key:`D`,text:`is rivalled by private medical services`}],answer:`B`,explanation:`第1段：“When it was established, the National Health Service (NHS) was visionary: offering high-quality, timely care to meet the dominant needs of the population it served.”。该句表述与选项“can hardly satisfy people's needs”一致，故选 B。`,evidence:{paragraphId:`p2-1`,quote:`When it was established, the National Health Service (NHS) was visionary: offering high-quality, timely care to meet the dominant needs of the population it served.`},score:2},{id:`kaoyan2-2025-real-r27`,number:27,type:`single`,stem:`One answer to the crisis in health and care is to ___`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`boost the efficiency of hospitals`},{key:`B`,text:`lighten the burden on social care`},{key:`C`,text:`increase resources for primary care`},{key:`D`,text:`reduce the pressure on communities`}],answer:`C`,explanation:`第3段：“Many of the answers to the crisis in health and care are well rehearsed.”。该句表述与选项“increase resources for primary care”一致，故选 C。`,evidence:{paragraphId:`p2-3`,quote:`Many of the answers to the crisis in health and care are well rehearsed.`},score:2},{id:`kaoyan2-2025-real-r28`,number:28,type:`single`,stem:`“Reimagining health” is aimed to ___`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`reinforce hospital management`},{key:`B`,text:`readjust healthcare regulations`},{key:`C`,text:`restructure the health system`},{key:`D`,text:`resume suspended health reforms`}],answer:`C`,explanation:`第4段：“That is why the Reform think tank is launching a new programme of work entitled “Reimagining health”, supported by ten former health ministers.”。该句表述与选项“restructure the health system”一致，故选 C。`,evidence:{paragraphId:`p2-4`,quote:`That is why the Reform think tank is launching a new programme of work entitled “Reimagining health”, supported by ten former health ministers.`},score:2},{id:`kaoyan2-2025-real-r29`,number:29,type:`single`,stem:`To maximise the nation's health, the author suggests ___`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`introducing relevant taxation policies`},{key:`B`,text:`paying due attention to social factors`},{key:`C`,text:`reevaluating major health outcomes`},{key:`D`,text:`enhancing the quality of health care`}],answer:`B`,explanation:`第5段：“This must begin with the question of how we maximise the health of the nation, rather than “fix” the NHS.”。该句表述与选项“paying due attention to social factors”一致，故选 B。`,evidence:{paragraphId:`p2-5`,quote:`This must begin with the question of how we maximise the health of the nation, rather than “fix” the NHS.`},score:2},{id:`kaoyan2-2025-real-r30`,number:30,type:`single`,stem:`It can be inferred that local leaders should ___`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`exercise their power more reasonably`},{key:`B`,text:`develop a stronger sense of responsibility`},{key:`C`,text:`play a bigger role in the health system`},{key:`D`,text:`understand people's health needs better`}],answer:`C`,explanation:`第6段：“What health functions should remain at the centre, and what should be given to local leaders, often responsible for services that create health, and with a much better understanding of the needs of…”。该句表述与选项“play a bigger role in the health system”一致，故选 C。`,evidence:{paragraphId:`p2-6`,quote:`What health functions should remain at the centre, and what should be given to local leaders, often responsible for services that create health, and with a much better understanding of the needs of…`},score:2},{id:`kaoyan2-2025-real-r31`,number:31,type:`single`,stem:`According to Paragraph 1, Nagpur's plan proposes measures to ___`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`tackle extreme weather`},{key:`B`,text:`ensure construction quality`},{key:`C`,text:`monitor emergency warnings`},{key:`D`,text:`address excessive workloads`}],answer:`A`,explanation:`第1段：“Nagpur's plan, for instance, calls for hospitals to set aside “cold wards” in the summer for treating heatstroke patients, and advises builders to give construction laborers a break from work on very…”。该句表述与选项“tackle extreme weather”一致，故选 A。`,evidence:{paragraphId:`p3-1`,quote:`Nagpur's plan, for instance, calls for hospitals to set aside “cold wards” in the summer for treating heatstroke patients, and advises builders to give construction laborers a break from work on very…`},score:2},{id:`kaoyan2-2025-real-r32`,number:32,type:`single`,stem:`One problem with existing HAPs is that they ___`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`prove too costly to be implemented`},{key:`B`,text:`lack localized alert-issuing criteria`},{key:`C`,text:`give delayed responses to heat waves`},{key:`D`,text:`keep hospitals under great pressure`}],answer:`B`,explanation:`第2段：“But implementation of existing HAPs has been uneven, according to a report from the Center for Policy Research.”。该句表述与选项“lack localized alert-issuing criteria”一致，故选 B。`,evidence:{paragraphId:`p3-2`,quote:`But implementation of existing HAPs has been uneven, according to a report from the Center for Policy Research.`},score:2},{id:`kaoyan2-2025-real-r33`,number:33,type:`single`,stem:`Mumbai's case shows that India's heat alert systems need to ___`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`include other factors besides temperature`},{key:`B`,text:`take subtle weather changes into account`},{key:`C`,text:`prioritize potentially disastrous heat waves`},{key:`D`,text:`draw further support from local authorities`}],answer:`A`,explanation:`第3段：“Mumbai's April heat stroke deaths highlighted the need for more nuanced and localized warnings, researchers say.”。该句表述与选项“include other factors besides temperature”一致，故选 A。`,evidence:{paragraphId:`p3-3`,quote:`Mumbai's April heat stroke deaths highlighted the need for more nuanced and localized warnings, researchers say.`},score:2},{id:`kaoyan2-2025-real-r34`,number:34,type:`single`,stem:`Kotharkar holds that a vulnerability map can help ___`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`prevent the harm of high humidity`},{key:`B`,text:`target areas needing special attention`},{key:`C`,text:`expand the Nagpur project's coverage`},{key:`D`,text:`make relief plans for heat-stricken people`}],answer:`B`,explanation:`第4段：“Among other things, she says, all cities should create a vulnerability map to help focus responses on the populations most at risk.”。该句表述与选项“target areas needing special attention”一致，故选 B。`,evidence:{paragraphId:`p3-4`,quote:`Among other things, she says, all cities should create a vulnerability map to help focus responses on the populations most at risk.`},score:2},{id:`kaoyan2-2025-real-r35`,number:35,type:`single`,stem:`According to the last paragraph, researchers suggest that HAPs should ___`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`focus more on the heatstroke treatment`},{key:`B`,text:`invite wider public participation`},{key:`C`,text:`apply for more government grants`},{key:`D`,text:`serve a broader range of purposes`}],answer:`D`,explanation:`第6段：“HAPs shouldn't just include short-term emergency responses, researchers say, but also recommend medium- to long-term measures that could make communities cooler.”。该句表述与选项“serve a broader range of purposes”一致，故选 D。`,evidence:{paragraphId:`p3-6`,quote:`HAPs shouldn't just include short-term emergency responses, researchers say, but also recommend medium- to long-term measures that could make communities cooler.`},score:2},{id:`kaoyan2-2025-real-r36`,number:36,type:`single`,stem:`According to Paragraph 1, desire paths are a result of ___`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`the curiosity to explore surrounding hills`},{key:`B`,text:`the necessity to preserve green spaces`},{key:`C`,text:`the tendency to pursue convenience`},{key:`D`,text:`the wish to find comfort in solitude`}],answer:`C`,explanation:`第1段：“Navigating beyond the organised pavements and parks of our urban spaces, desire paths are the unofficial footprints of a community, revealing the unspoken preferences, shared shortcuts and collective…”。该句表述与选项“the tendency to pursue convenience”一致，故选 C。`,evidence:{paragraphId:`p4-1`,quote:`Navigating beyond the organised pavements and parks of our urban spaces, desire paths are the unofficial footprints of a community, revealing the unspoken preferences, shared shortcuts and collective…`},score:2},{id:`kaoyan2-2025-real-r37`,number:37,type:`single`,stem:`It can be inferred that Ohio State University ___`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`intends to improve its desire paths`},{key:`B`,text:`leads in the research on desire paths`},{key:`C`,text:`guides the creation of its desire paths`},{key:`D`,text:`takes a positive view of desire paths`}],answer:`D`,explanation:`第2段：“Ohio State University allowed its students to navigate the Oval, a lawn in the centre of campus, freely, then proceeded to pave the desire paths, creating a web of effective routes students had…”。该句表述与选项“takes a positive view of desire paths”一致，故选 D。`,evidence:{paragraphId:`p4-2`,quote:`Ohio State University allowed its students to navigate the Oval, a lawn in the centre of campus, freely, then proceeded to pave the desire paths, creating a web of effective routes students had…`},score:2},{id:`kaoyan2-2025-real-r38`,number:38,type:`single`,stem:`The images on the Reddit webpage reflect ___`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`conflicting opinions on the use of desire paths`},{key:`B`,text:`the call to upgrade the designing of public spaces`},{key:`C`,text:`the demand for proper planning of desire paths`},{key:`D`,text:`growing concerns over the loss of public spaces`}],answer:`A`,explanation:`第3段：“A Reddit webpage devoted to the phenomenon, boasting nearly 50,000 members, showcases images of local desire paths adorned with signs instructing pedestrians to adhere to designated walkways,…”。该句表述与选项“conflicting opinions on the use of desire paths”一致，故选 A。`,evidence:{paragraphId:`p4-3`,quote:`A Reddit webpage devoted to the phenomenon, boasting nearly 50,000 members, showcases images of local desire paths adorned with signs instructing pedestrians to adhere to designated walkways,…`},score:2},{id:`kaoyan2-2025-real-r39`,number:39,type:`single`,stem:`The example of the Wickquasgeck Trail illustrates ___`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`the growth of New York City`},{key:`B`,text:`the Dutch origin of desire paths`},{key:`C`,text:`the importance of urban planning`},{key:`D`,text:`the recognition of desire paths`}],answer:`D`,explanation:`第4段：“The Wickquasgeck Trail is an example of a historical desire path, created by Native Americans to cross the forests of Manhattan and move between settlements quickly.”。该句表述与选项“the recognition of desire paths”一致，故选 D。`,evidence:{paragraphId:`p4-4`,quote:`The Wickquasgeck Trail is an example of a historical desire path, created by Native Americans to cross the forests of Manhattan and move between settlements quickly.`},score:2},{id:`kaoyan2-2025-real-r40`,number:40,type:`single`,stem:`It can be learned from the last paragraph that desire paths ___`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`reveal humans' deep respect for nature`},{key:`B`,text:`are crucial to humans' mental well-being`},{key:`C`,text:`are a human imitation of animal behaviour`},{key:`D`,text:`show a shared trait in humans and animals`}],answer:`D`,explanation:`第6段：“Animal desire paths, such as ducks forging trails through frozen ponds or dogs carving direct routes in gardens, highlight the adaptability of these trails in both human and animal experiences.”。该句表述与选项“show a shared trait in humans and animals”一致，故选 D。`,evidence:{paragraphId:`p4-6`,quote:`Animal desire paths, such as ducks forging trails through frozen ponds or dogs carving direct routes in gardens, highlight the adaptability of these trails in both human and animal experiences.`},score:2}]},{id:`newtype`,kind:`reading`,title:`Section II  Reading Comprehension  Part B`,instructions:`Directions: Read the following text and answer the questions by choosing the most suitable subheading from the list A-G for each of the numbered paragraphs (41-45). There are two extra subheadings which you do not need to use. Mark your answers on the ANSWER SHEET. (10 points)`,minutes:15,passages:[{id:`p1`,title:`Five Steps to Suggesting a Change at Work That'll Actually Get Taken Seriously`,paragraphs:[{id:`p1-1`,text:`Everyone wants to be that person-the one who looks at the same information as everyone else, but who sees a fresh, innovative solution. However, it takes more than simply having a good idea. How you share it is as important as the suggestion itself. Why? Because writing a new script-literally or figuratively-means that other team members will have to adapt to something new. So whether you're suggesting a (seemingly) benign change like streamlining outdated protocol, or a bigger change like adding an hour to each workday so people can leave early on Fridays, you're asking others to reimagine their workflow or schedule. Not to mention, if the process you're scrapping is one someone else suggested, there's the possibility of hurt feelings. To gain buy-in on an innovative, new idea, follow these steps:`}]}],bank:{A:`Stay positive`,B:`Respect the past`,C:`Use channels`,D:`Give it time`,E:`Invite resistance`,F:`Be a salesman`,G:`Be humble`},questions:[{id:`kaoyan2-2025-real-n41`,number:41,type:`bank`,stem:`Great ideas don't stand alone. In other words, you can't mention your suggestion once and expect it to be adopted. To see a change, you'll need to champion your plan and sell its merits. In addition, you need to be willing to stand up to scrutiny and criticism and be prepared to explain your innovation in different ways for various audiences.`,answer:`F`,explanation:`本段：“In addition, you need to be willing to stand up to scrutiny and criticism and be prepared to explain your innovation in different ways for various audiences.”，该段主旨与小标题“Be a salesman”对应，故选 F。`,score:2},{id:`kaoyan2-2025-real-n42`,number:42,type:`bank`,stem:`Sometimes it makes sense to go to your boss first. But other times, it's useful to build a coalition among your co-workers or other stakeholders. When it works, it works great-because you're ready for your stubborn supervisor's pushback with answers like, “Actually, I connected with a few people in our tech department to discuss how much time these kinds of website updates would take, and they suggested they have the bandwidth.”`,answer:`C`,explanation:`本段：“When it works, it works great-because you're ready for your stubborn supervisor's pushback with answers like, “Actually, I connected with a few people in our tech department to discuss how much time…”，该段主旨与小标题“Use channels”对应，故选 C。`,score:2},{id:`kaoyan2-2025-real-n43`,number:43,type:`bank`,stem:`One of the biggest barriers to gaining buy-in occurs when the owner of an idea is viewed as argumentative, defensive, or close-minded. Because, let's be honest: No one likes a know-it-all. So, if people disagree with you, don't be indignant. Instead, listen to their concerns fully, try to understand their perspective, and include their concerns (and possible remedies) in future discussions. So, instead of saying, “Martha, our current slogan is confusing and should be updated,” you could try, “Martha raises a great point that our current slogan has a long history for our stakeholders, but I wonder if we might be able to brainstorm a tagline that could build on that-and be clearer for new customers.”`,answer:`G`,explanation:`本段：“So, instead of saying, “Martha, our current slogan is confusing and should be updated,” you could try, “Martha raises a great point that our current slogan has a long history for our stakeholders,…”，该段主旨与小标题“Be humble”对应，故选 G。`,score:2},{id:`kaoyan2-2025-real-n44`,number:44,type:`bank`,stem:`New ideas are the grandchildren of old ones. In other words, don't throw old solutions under the bus to make your improvement stand out. Remember that in light of whatever the problem the old system solved-or, maybe, has failed to solve in recent memory-it was a great idea at the time. Appreciating the older contributions as you suggest future innovations helps bolster the credibility of your idea.`,answer:`B`,explanation:`本段：“Remember that in light of whatever the problem the old system solved-or, maybe, has failed to solve in recent memory-it was a great idea at the time.”，该段主旨与小标题“Respect the past”对应，故选 B。`,score:2},{id:`kaoyan2-2025-real-n45`,number:45,type:`bank`,stem:`When pitching a new idea, it's important to use the language of abundance instead of the language of deficit. Instead of saying what is wrong, broken, or suboptimal, talk about what is right, fixable, or ideal. For example, try, “I can see lots of applications for this new approach” rather than, “This innovation is the only way.” Be optimistic but realistic, and you will stand out.`,answer:`A`,explanation:`本段：“For example, try, “I can see lots of applications for this new approach” rather than, “This innovation is the only way.” Be optimistic but realistic, and you will stand out.”，该段主旨与小标题“Stay positive”对应，故选 A。`,score:2}]},{id:`translation`,kind:`translation`,title:`Section III  Translation`,instructions:`Directions: Translate the following text into Chinese. Write your translation on the ANSWER SHEET. (15 points)`,minutes:25,questions:[{id:`kaoyan2-2025-real-t46`,number:46,type:`translation`,stem:`You know the moment-the conversation slows, then there's a pause. It's awkward, and so awkward that some people will panic and say anything. Do we all find such silences so stressful? Researchers analysed the frequency and impact of gaps greater than 2 seconds during conversations, including an overview of previous studies which indicate that the fear of awkward silences can be so extreme that people avoid talking to strangers, even though doing so is likely to be an enjoyable experience. During conversations with short gaps, people feel more connected to their conversation partners. But such feelings of connection markedly dip when entering a long gap. Long gaps between strangers are likely to be followed by a change in topic. But the opposite seems to be true for conversations between friends. Long gaps there saw increased connection. Between friends, longer gaps seem to provide natural moments for reflection and expression.`,answer:`参考译文`,explanation:`参考译文：你知道那样的时刻：谈话慢了下来，随后出现停顿。这很尴尬，而且尴尬到有些人会慌张起来，随便说些什么。我们都会觉得这样的沉默如此令人紧张吗？研究人员分析了谈话中超过2秒的空隙出现的频率及其影响，其中还概述了以往研究。这些研究表明，对尴尬沉默的恐惧可能极其强烈，以至于人们会避免与陌生人交谈，尽管这样做很可能是一种愉快的体验。在停顿较短的谈话中，人们会感觉与谈话对象联系更紧密。但当进入较长停顿时，这种联系感会明显下降。陌生人之间出现较长停顿后，很可能会换一个话题。但朋友之间的谈话似乎正相反。朋友之间较长的停顿会带来更强的联系感。对朋友而言，较长的停顿似乎提供了自然的反思和表达时刻。`,score:15}],reference:{translation:`你知道那样的时刻：谈话慢了下来，随后出现停顿。这很尴尬，而且尴尬到有些人会慌张起来，随便说些什么。我们都会觉得这样的沉默如此令人紧张吗？研究人员分析了谈话中超过2秒的空隙出现的频率及其影响，其中还概述了以往研究。这些研究表明，对尴尬沉默的恐惧可能极其强烈，以至于人们会避免与陌生人交谈，尽管这样做很可能是一种愉快的体验。在停顿较短的谈话中，人们会感觉与谈话对象联系更紧密。但当进入较长停顿时，这种联系感会明显下降。陌生人之间出现较长停顿后，很可能会换一个话题。但朋友之间的谈话似乎正相反。朋友之间较长的停顿会带来更强的联系感。对朋友而言，较长的停顿似乎提供了自然的反思和表达时刻。`}},{id:`writing1`,kind:`writing`,title:`Section IV  Writing  Part A`,instructions:`Suppose you are planning a short play based on a classic Chinese novel. Write your friend John an email to 1) introduce the play, and 2) invite him to take part in it. Write your answer in about 100 words on the ANSWER SHEET. Do not sign your own name in your email; use “Li Ming” instead. (10 points)`,minutes:20,questions:[{id:`kaoyan2-2025-real-w47`,number:47,type:`writing`,stem:`Suppose you are planning a short play based on a classic Chinese novel. Write your friend John an email to 1) introduce the play, and 2) invite him to take part in it. Write your answer in about 100 words on the ANSWER SHEET. Do not sign your own name in your email; use “Li Ming” instead. (10 points)`,answer:`见参考范文`,explanation:`写作任务：给John写邮件，介绍根据中国古典小说改编的短剧并邀请他参加。按 Directions 规定的字数与署名要求作答；语言要点与结构可参考下方「参考范文」。`,score:10}],reference:{essay:`Dear John, I am writing with sincerity to inform you of some necessary information about a short play based on a classic Chinese novel. I am going to hold it in order to shed light on some Chinese conventional cultures. It is a fantastic and inspiring play, from which you can learn an essential quality for life — persistence, and I am writing in hope that you could attend the activity as an amateur. The play is scheduled to be held in the No. 2 Lecture Hall at 7o’clock in the evening, December 28th, 2024. Your attendance would be a great honor to me. Were there anything unclear, please do not hesitate to contact me at Liming@mail.com. Yours sincerely, Li Ming`}},{id:`writing2`,kind:`writing`,title:`Section IV  Writing  Part B`,instructions:`Write an essay based on the chart below. In your essay, you should 1) describe and interpret the chart, and 2) give your comments. Write your answer in about 150 words on the ANSWER SHEET. (15 points)`,minutes:30,questions:[{id:`kaoyan2-2025-real-w48`,number:48,type:`writing`,stem:`Write an essay based on the chart below. In your essay, you should 1) describe and interpret the chart, and 2) give your comments. Write your answer in about 150 words on the ANSWER SHEET. (15 points)`,answer:`见参考范文`,explanation:`写作任务：柱状图显示某社区老年人主要日常休闲活动调查：看电视90.8%，散步68.3%，养花34.7%，阅读31.8%，下棋18.4%。按 Directions 规定的字数作答，围绕图表/图画描述、阐释与评论展开；参考范文见下方。`,score:15}],reference:{essay:`The bar chart clearly presents different proportions concerning the main daily leisure activities of the elderly in a community. As can be seen, the proportions of watching TV, taking a walk, growing flowers and playing chess are 90.8%, 86.3%, 34.7% and 18.4% respectively. What is noticeable is that reading books accounts for 31.8%. The portrayal is designed to awaken us to the social phenomenon of leisure activities for the elderly, which is not uncommon in this day and age. There exist multiple reasons behind this phenomenon. First of all, due to the prosperity of economy in China and the increase of residents’ income in recent decades, a large body of old people are paying more attention to colorful and comfortable life style, which boosts the diversification of leisure activities. Here is a story. Even more the aged are willing to take a walk, grow flowers and play chess with their family. In addition, we have to admit that plenty of spare time also motivates old people to read more books or watch TV, which brings about a far-reaching impact on their old daily lives. Based on the above-mentioned analysis, we may safely arrive at a conclusion that the trend is an inevitable result of multiple daily leisure activities for senior citizens. Hence, there is every reason to believe it will keep going in the foreseeable future.`}}]},"kaoyan2-2024-real":{subtitle:`2024 年 · 站内收录`,minutes:180,words:4200,tags:[`真题`,`考研英语二`],summary:`2024 年考研英语（二）真题站内收录：完形填空、四篇阅读理解、新题型、段落翻译与两篇写作全部题面、选项与参考答案，解析基于公开解析资料与原文定位整理；答案为公开渠道汇总的非官方参考答案。`,parts:[{id:`cloze`,kind:`cloze`,title:`Section I  Use of English`,instructions:`Directions: Read the following text. Choose the best word(s) for each numbered blank and mark A, B, C or D on the ANSWER SHEET. (10 points)`,minutes:20,questions:[{id:`kaoyan2-2024-real-c1`,number:1,type:`single`,stem:`Some of us feel energised by spending lots of time with others, ___1___ some of us may feel drained, even if it's doing something we enjoy.`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`because`},{key:`B`,text:`unless`},{key:`C`,text:`whereas`},{key:`D`,text:`until`}],answer:`C`,explanation:`答案 C。本题空格前后都为主谓宾齐全的完整句子, 并且选项为连词, 考查空格前后句子之间的逻辑关系。前面分句中的energized(充满热情的)和后句中的drained (筋疲力尽的)构成转折关系, 故正确答案为 whereas。`,score:.5},{id:`kaoyan2-2024-real-c2`,number:2,type:`single`,stem:`This is why finding a ___2___ in your social life is key.`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`contrast`},{key:`B`,text:`balance`},{key:`C`,text:`link`},{key:`D`,text:`gap`}],answer:`B`,explanation:`答案 B。本题填入名词充当finding的宾语,虽然句子本身较为简单但线索较远,需结合上下文。上文中说到不同的人对social life的感觉不一样,有人充满热情,有人感到疲惫:以及下文中 spending too much time on your own花太多时间独处”和第四段“to have too much of a social life 进行过多社交”,可知本文讨论的应该是“找到社交生活的平衡”,故正确答案为balance。`,score:.5},{id:`kaoyan2-2024-real-c3`,number:3,type:`single`,stem:`Spending too much time on your own, not ___3___ others, can make you feel lonely and ___4___.`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`seeing`},{key:`B`,text:`pleasing`},{key:`C`,text:`judging`},{key:`D`,text:`teaching`}],answer:`A`,explanation:`答案 A。根据前文“spending too much time on your own”可知 not seeing others不与别人见面”,故正确答案为seeing。`,score:.5},{id:`kaoyan2-2024-real-c4`,number:4,type:`single`,stem:`Spending too much time on your own, not ___3___ others, can make you feel lonely and ___4___.`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`misguided`},{key:`B`,text:`surprised`},{key:`C`,text:`spoiled`},{key:`D`,text:`disconnected`}],answer:`D`,explanation:`答案 D。本题空格处与“lonely” 构成并列关系 , 故正确答案为 disconnected“与世隔绝的”。`,score:.5},{id:`kaoyan2-2024-real-c5`,number:5,type:`single`,stem:`Loneliness is known to impact on your mental health and ___5___ a low mood.`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`contribute to`},{key:`B`,text:`rely on`},{key:`C`,text:`interfere with`},{key:`D`,text:`go against`}],answer:`A`,explanation:`答案 A。本题空格处填入谓语动词, 其主语为Loneliness, 宾语为 a low mood“情绪低落”, 根据主谓宾搭配, 正确答案为“contribute to 导致, 促成”。整个句子意思为“孤独导致情绪低落”。其他选项“rely on 依赖,“interfere with 干扰”,“go against 违背,反对”皆不符合语境。`,score:.5},{id:`kaoyan2-2024-real-c6`,number:6,type:`single`,stem:`This might be especially true if, ___6___, you are working from home and you are ___7___ on the usual social conversations that happen in an office.`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`in fact`},{key:`B`,text:`of course`},{key:`C`,text:`for example`},{key:`D`,text:`on average`}],answer:`C`,explanation:`答案 C。本题考察逻辑关系中的列举关系,空格前表达 this might be especially true,概括表达这种情况是真是存在的,if 条件句中说具体情况在家工作,前概括后具体,是用的列举的逻辑关系故 C. for example 正确,其他三个选项分别为:in fact 事实上,实际上,of course 当然, 自然,on average 基本上, 平均起来, 都不符合文意。`,score:.5},{id:`kaoyan2-2024-real-c7`,number:7,type:`single`,stem:`This might be especially true if, ___6___, you are working from home and you are ___7___ on the usual social conversations that happen in an office.`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`cutting back`},{key:`B`,text:`missing out`},{key:`C`,text:`breaking in`},{key:`D`,text:`looking down`}],answer:`B`,explanation:`答案 B。本题考察逻辑关系中的并列关系,第7题所在句子是由and并列在一起的两个并列句,前一句讲you are working from home你在家工作,后一句表达的主语you和后面的the usual social conversations that happen in an office(办公室里常见的社交对话)得是没能进行才可以,这样并列句之间才能保持意义致性,所以本题选择B. miss out 与on是固定搭配错过,错失。其他三个选项分别为:cut back on 减少, 降低;break in on 打断;look down on 看不起, 都不符合文意。`,score:.5},{id:`kaoyan2-2024-real-c8`,number:8,type:`single`,stem:`Other life changes can ___8___ periods of loneliness too, such as retirement, changing jobs or becoming a parent.`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`shorten`},{key:`B`,text:`trigger`},{key:`C`,text:`follow`},{key:`D`,text:`interrupt`}],answer:`B`,explanation:`答案 B。本题考察成分搭配关系,需要选择动词,主语为 Other life changes其他生活变化, 宾语为periods of loneliness孤独时期, 意为: 其他生活变化也会引发孤独时期,故选择B trigger 。其他选项为: shorten 缩短,follow 紧跟着,interrupt 解释,都不符合文意。`,score:.5},{id:`kaoyan2-2024-real-c9`,number:9,type:`single`,stem:`There are ways to ___9___ a social life, but it can feel overwhelming ___10___.`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`assess`},{key:`B`,text:`interpret`},{key:`C`,text:`provide`},{key:`D`,text:`regain`}],answer:`D`,explanation:`答案 D。本题考察词义辨析,前一句在讲认识到孤独感很重要,后面有些方法和社会生活之间的关系,应该是获得,接近社会生活,故选 regain, 获得, 其他选项access 评估,interpret 解释,provide 提供,不合符文意。`,score:.5},{id:`kaoyan2-2024-real-c10`,number:10,type:`single`,stem:`There are ways to ___9___ a social life, but it can feel overwhelming ___10___.`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`at first`},{key:`B`,text:`in turn`},{key:`C`,text:`on time`},{key:`D`,text:`by chance`}],answer:`A`,explanation:`答案 A。There are ways to regain a social life, but it can feel over whelming at first.前半句重新获得社交生活,所以后半句说是刚开始会感觉到过于乏味,前后句在逻辑上是一种顺承关系。其它选项:in turn 轮流依次;on time 按时,by chance 碰巧,偶然,不合符文意。`,score:.5},{id:`kaoyan2-2024-real-c11`,number:11,type:`single`,stem:`You can then find groups and activities related to those where you will be able to meet ___11___ people.`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`far-sighted`},{key:`B`,text:`strong-willed`},{key:`C`,text:`kind-hearted`},{key:`D`,text:`like-minded`}],answer:`D`,explanation:`答案 D。本题根据上文主题解决“个人孤独问题”,Its a great idea to start by thinking about hobbies you enjoy.“ 开始思考你喜欢的爱好” 下文又写到 find groups..... 说明此处应该是遇见“想法相似的”人, 选择like-minded。`,score:.5},{id:`kaoyan2-2024-real-c12`,number:12,type:`single`,stem:`There are groups aimed at new parents, at those who want to ___12___ a new sport for the first time, or networking events for those in the same profession to meet up and ___13___ ideas.`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`try`},{key:`B`,text:`promote`},{key:`C`,text:`watch`},{key:`D`,text:`describe`}],answer:`A`,explanation:`答案 A。本题结合上文“找想法相似的人”,再结合句子内部动宾短语搭配, 能和 sport 搭配且符合上下文句意的只有 try。其他三个选项 B. promote“促进”,C. watch“观看”,D. describe“描述”均不符合文意。`,score:.5},{id:`kaoyan2-2024-real-c13`,number:13,type:`single`,stem:`There are groups aimed at new parents, at those who want to ___12___ a new sport for the first time, or networking events for those in the same profession to meet up and ___13___ ideas.`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`test`},{key:`B`,text:`share`},{key:`C`,text:`accept`},{key:`D`,text:`revise`}],answer:`B`,explanation:`答案 B。本题考察句子内部 and 前后并列一致逻辑关系,和 meet up 语义最接近的选项是 share.分享(观点)。其余三个选项 A. test“测试”,与 dea 搭配不当:C. accept“接受”和 D. revise“修正,改进” 与上下文语意不搭。`,score:.5},{id:`kaoyan2-2024-real-c14`,number:14,type:`single`,stem:`On the other hand, it's ___14___ possible to have too much of a social life.`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`already`},{key:`B`,text:`thus`},{key:`C`,text:`also`},{key:`D`,text:`only`}],answer:`C`,explanation:`答案 C。本题前文中的 on the other hand 说明与上文之间是并列逻辑关系, 因此最佳选项选C. also.其余选项,A. already 强调时间先后顺序,B. thus 表示结果,D. only 表示强调,均不符合文意。`,score:.5},{id:`kaoyan2-2024-real-c15`,number:15,type:`single`,stem:`If you feel like you're always doing something and there is never any ___15___ in your calendar for downtime, you could suffer social burnout or social ___16___.`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`list`},{key:`B`,text:`order`},{key:`C`,text:`space`},{key:`D`,text:`boundary`}],answer:`C`,explanation:`答案 C。本题所在句子中 you're always doing something 与 there is never any 15 in your calendar之间构成and 并列一致关系,能满足致关系的只有 space, 其余选项 A. list“清单”,B. order“顺序”,D. boundary“边界”,均语意不符。`,score:.5},{id:`kaoyan2-2024-real-c16`,number:16,type:`single`,stem:`If you feel like you're always doing something and there is never any ___15___ in your calendar for downtime, you could suffer social burnout or social ___16___.`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`fatigue`},{key:`B`,text:`criticism`},{key:`C`,text:`injustice`},{key:`D`,text:`dilemma`}],answer:`A`,explanation:`答案 A。本题通过句内并列连词or, 判断 social 和 social burnout 是并列成分,其中空格对应burnout“疲惫”,选择fatigue。`,score:.5},{id:`kaoyan2-2024-real-c17`,number:17,type:`single`,stem:`Low mood, low energy, irritability and trouble sleeping could all be ___17___ of poor social health.`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`sources`},{key:`B`,text:`standards`},{key:`C`,text:`signs`},{key:`D`,text:`scores`}],answer:`C`,explanation:`答案 C。本题中空格作表语,根据主系表搭配关系,主语low mood, low energy, irritability and trouble sleeping “情绪低落、能量不足、易怒、失眠”空格后有修饰语 poor social health “社交能力差”,可知前者是后者的“迹象”。`,score:.5},{id:`kaoyan2-2024-real-c18`,number:18,type:`single`,stem:`Make sure you ___18___ some time in your diary when you're ___19___ for socialising and use this time to relax, ___20___ and recover.`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`take over`},{key:`B`,text:`wipe off`},{key:`C`,text:`add up`},{key:`D`,text:`mark out`}],answer:`D`,explanation:`答案 D。本题空格处作谓语,体现主宾之间关系, “当你...社交时, 确保在你的日程表中,...一些时间”A. turn over 接; B. wipe off 消灭; C. add up 把...加起来; D. mark out 划分出:“你”和“时间之间. 按照搭配关系,应当是“你划分出一些时间”。`,score:.5},{id:`kaoyan2-2024-real-c19`,number:19,type:`single`,stem:`Make sure you ___18___ some time in your diary when you're ___19___ for socialising and use this time to relax, ___20___ and recover.`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`ungrateful`},{key:`B`,text:`unavailable`},{key:`C`,text:`responsible`},{key:`D`,text:`regretful`}],answer:`B`,explanation:`答案 B。本题通过句内语义可知, 主句: 在日程表中划分出一些时间, 是在你“没空”社交时, 选择unavailable。ungrateful:a.不领情的; 忘恩负义的;responsible:a.负责任的;regretful:a.后悔的, 遗憾的; 均不符合语义。`,score:.5},{id:`kaoyan2-2024-real-c20`,number:20,type:`single`,stem:`Make sure you ___18___ some time in your diary when you're ___19___ for socialising and use this time to relax, ___20___ and recover.`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`react`},{key:`B`,text:`repeat`},{key:`C`,text:`return`},{key:`D`,text:`rest`}],answer:`D`,explanation:`答案 D。本题空格处和relax,recover构成并列关系“放松”,“恢复”和 rest“休息”,属于相关语义。`,score:.5}]},{id:`reading`,kind:`reading`,title:`Section II  Reading Comprehension  Part A`,instructions:`Directions: Read the following four texts. Answer the questions below each text by choosing A, B, C or D. Mark your answers on the ANSWER SHEET. (40 points)`,minutes:70,passages:[{id:`p1`,title:`Text 1`,paragraphs:[{id:`p1-1`,marker:`1`,text:`In her new book Cogs and Monsters: What Economics Is, and What It Should Be, Diane Coyle, an economist at Cambridge University, argues that the digital economy requires new ways of thinking about progress. “Whatever we mean by the economy growing, by things getting better, the gains will have to be more evenly shared than in the recent past,” she writes. “An economy of tech millionaires or billionaires and gig workers, with middle-income jobs undercut by automation, will not be politically sustainable.”`},{id:`p1-2`,marker:`2`,text:`Improving living standards and increasing prosperity for more people will require greater use of digital technologies to boost productivity in various sectors, including health care and construction, says Coyle. But people can't be expected to embrace the changes if they're not seeing the benefits - if they're just seeing good jobs being destroyed.`},{id:`p1-3`,marker:`3`,text:`In a recent interview, Coyle said she fears that tech's inequality problem could be a roadblock to deploying AI. “We're talking about disruption,” she says. “These are transformative technologies that change the ways we spend our time every day, that change business models that succeed.” To make such “tremendous changes,” she adds, you need social buy-in.`},{id:`p1-4`,marker:`4`,text:`Instead, says Coyle, resentment is simmering among many as the benefits are perceived to go to elites in a handful of prosperous cities.`},{id:`p1-5`,marker:`5`,text:`According to the Brookings Institution, a short list of eight American cities that included San Francisco, San Jose, Boston, and Seattle had roughly 38% of all tech jobs by 2019. New AI technologies are particularly concentrated: Brookings's Mark Muro and Sifan Liu estimate that just 15 cities account for two-thirds of the AI assets and capabilities in the United States.`},{id:`p1-6`,marker:`6`,text:`The dominance of a few cities in the invention and commercialization of AI means that geographical disparities in wealth will continue to soar. Not only will this foster political and social unrest, but it could, as Coyle suggests, hold back the sorts of AI technologies needed for regional economies to grow.`},{id:`p1-7`,marker:`7`,text:`Part of the solution could lie in somehow loosening the stranglehold that Big Tech has on defining the AI agenda. That will likely take increased federal funding for research independent of the tech giants.`},{id:`p1-8`,marker:`8`,text:`A more immediate response is to broaden our digital imaginations to conceive of AI technologies that don't simply replace jobs but expand opportunities in the sectors that different parts of the country care most about, like health care, education, and manufacturing.`}]},{id:`p2`,title:`Text 2`,paragraphs:[{id:`p2-1`,marker:`1`,text:`The UK is facing a future construction crisis because of a failure to plant trees to produce wood, Confor has warned. The forestry and wood trade body has called for urgent action to reduce the country's reliance on timber imports and provide a stable supply of wood for future generations. Currently only 20 per cent of the UK's wood requirement is home-grown while it remains the second-largest net importer of timber in the world.`},{id:`p2-2`,marker:`2`,text:`Coming at a time of fresh incentives from the UK government for landowners to grow more trees, the trade body says these don't go far enough and fail to promote the benefits of planting them to boost timber supplies. “Not only are we facing a carbon crisis now, but we will also be facing a future construction crisis because of a failure to plant trees to produce wood,” said Stuart Goodall, chief executive of Confor. “For decades we have not taken responsibility for investing in our domestic wood supply, leaving us exposed to fluctuating prices and fighting for future supplies of wood as global demand rises and our own supplies fall.”`},{id:`p2-3`,marker:`3`,text:`The UK has ideal conditions for growing wood to build low-carbon homes and is a global leader in certifying that its forests are sustainably managed, Confor says. While around three quarters of Scottish homes are built from Scottish timber, the use of home-grown wood in England is only around 25 per cent. The causes of the UK's current position are complex and range from outdated perceptions of productive forestry to the decimation of trees by grey squirrels. It also encompasses significant hesitation on behalf of farmers and other landowners to invest in longer-term planting projects.`},{id:`p2-4`,marker:`4`,text:`While productive tree planting can deliver real financial benefits to rural economies and contribute to the UK's net-zero strategy, the focus of government support continues to be on food production and the rewilding and planting of native woodland solely for biodiversity. Goodall added: “While food production and biodiversity health are clearly of critical importance, we need our land to also provide secure supplies of wood for construction, manufacturing and contribute to net zero.”`},{id:`p2-5`,marker:`5`,text:`“While the UK government has stated its ambition for more tree planting, there has been little action on the ground. Confor is now calling for much greater impetus behind those aspirations to ensure we have enough wood to meet increasing demand.”`}]},{id:`p3`,title:`Text 3`,paragraphs:[{id:`p3-1`,marker:`1`,text:`One of the biggest challenges in keeping unsafe aging drivers off the road is convincing them that it's time to turn over the keys. “It's a complete life-changer” when someone stops - or is forced to stop - driving, said former risk manager Anne M. Menke.`},{id:`p3-2`,marker:`2`,text:`“The American Medical Association advises physicians that ‘in situations where clear evidence of substantial driving impairment implies a strong threat to patient and public safety, and where the physician's advice to discontinue driving privileges is ignored, it is desirable and ethical to notify the Department of Motor Vehicles,’” Menke wrote. “Some states require physicians to report, others allow but do not mandate reports, while a few consider a report a breach of confidentiality. There could be liability and penalties if a physician does not act in accordance with state laws on reporting and confidentiality,” she counseled.`},{id:`p3-3`,marker:`3`,text:`Part of the problem in keeping older drivers safe is that the difficulties are addressed piecemeal by different professions with different focuses, including gerontologists, highway administration officials, automotive engineers and others, said gerontologist Elizabeth Dugan. “There's not a National Institute of Older Driver Studies,” she said. “We need better evidence on what makes drivers unsafe and what can help,” said Dugan.`},{id:`p3-4`,marker:`4`,text:`One thing that does seem to work is requiring drivers to report in person for license renewal. Mandatory in-person renewal was associated with a 31 per cent reduction in fatal crashes involving drivers 85 or older, according to one study. Passing vision tests also produced a similar decline in fatal crashes for those drivers, although there appeared to be no benefit from combining the two.`},{id:`p3-5`,marker:`5`,text:`Many older drivers don't see eye doctors or can't afford to. Primary care providers have their hands full and may not be able to follow through with patients who have trouble driving because they can't turn their heads or remember where they are going - or have gotten shorter and haven't changed their seat settings sufficiently to reach car pedals easily.`},{id:`p3-6`,marker:`6`,text:`As long as there are other cars on the roads, self-driving cars won't solve the problems of crashes, said Dugan. Avoiding dangers posed by all those human drivers would require too many algorithms, she said. But we need to do more to improve safety, said Dugan. “If we're going to have 100-year lives, we need cars that a 90-year old can drive comfortably.”`}]},{id:`p4`,title:`Text 4`,paragraphs:[{id:`p4-1`,marker:`1`,text:`If you look at the apps on your phone, chances are you have at least one related to your health - and probably several. Whether it is a mental health app, a fitness tracker, a connected health device or something else, many of us are taking advantage of this technology to keep better track of our health in some shape or form. Recent research found that 350,000 health apps were available on the market, 90,000 of which launched in 2020 alone.`},{id:`p4-2`,marker:`2`,text:`While these apps have a great deal to offer, it is not always clear how the personal information we input is collected, safeguarded and shared online. Existing health privacy law is primarily focused on the way hospitals, doctors' offices, clinics and insurance companies store health records online. The health information these apps and health data tracking wearables are collecting typically does not receive the same legal protections.`},{id:`p4-3`,marker:`3`,text:`Without additional protections in place, companies may share and potentially monetize personal health information in a way consumers may not have authorized or anticipated. In 2021, Flo Health faced a Federal Trade Commission (FTC) investigation. The FTC alleged in a complaint that “despite express privacy claims, the company took control of users' sensitive fertility data and shared it with third parties.” Flo Health and the FTC settled the matter with a Consent Order requiring the company to get app users' express affirmative consent before sharing their health information as well as to instruct the third parties to delete the data they had obtained.`},{id:`p4-4`,marker:`4`,text:`Section 5 of the FTC Act empowers the FTC to initiate enforcement action against unfair or deceptive acts, meaning the FTC can only act after the fact if a company's privacy practices are misleading or cause unjustified consumer harm. While the FTC is doing what it can to ensure apps are keeping their promises to consumers around the handling of their sensitive health information, the rate at which these health apps are hitting the market demonstrates just how immense of a challenge this is.`},{id:`p4-5`,marker:`5`,text:`As to the prospects for federal legislation, commentators suggest that comprehensive federal privacy legislation seems unlikely in the short term. States have begun implementing their own solutions to shore up protections for consumer-generated health data. California has been at the forefront of state privacy efforts with the California Consumer Privacy Act of 2018. Virginia, Colorado and Utah have also recently passed state consumer data privacy legislation.`}]}],questions:[{id:`kaoyan2-2024-real-r21`,number:21,type:`single`,stem:`Coyle argues in her new book that economic growth should ___.`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`give rise to innovations`},{key:`B`,text:`diversify career choices`},{key:`C`,text:`benefit people equally`},{key:`D`,text:`be promoted forcefully`}],answer:`C`,explanation:`答案 C。由题于定位到原文第一段。根据“Whatever we mean by the economy growing, by things getting better, the gains will have to be more evenly shared than in the recent past, “ she writes.”可知,Coyle 认为经济增长应该公平地惠及众生,因此选项 C 符合题意。`,evidence:{paragraphId:`p1-1`,quote:`In her new book Cogs and Monsters: What Economics Is, and What It Should Be, Diane Coyle, an economist at Cambridge University, argues that the digital economy requires new ways of thinking about…`},score:2},{id:`kaoyan2-2024-real-r22`,number:22,type:`single`,stem:`According to Paragraph 2, digital technologies should be used to ___.`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`bring about instant prosperity`},{key:`B`,text:`reduce people's workload`},{key:`C`,text:`raise overall work efficiency`},{key:`D`,text:`enhance cross-sector cooperation`}],answer:`C`,explanation:`答案 C。由题干定位到原文第二段第一句。原文指出: will require greater use of digital technologies to boost productivity in various sectors, 这表明应该用数字技术来提升个行业的生产率。因此选项 C 符合题意。`,evidence:{paragraphId:`p1-2`,quote:`Improving living standards and increasing prosperity for more people will require greater use of digital technologies to boost productivity in various sectors, including health care and construction,…`},score:2},{id:`kaoyan2-2024-real-r23`,number:23,type:`single`,stem:`What does Coyle fear about transformative technologies?`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`They may affect work-life balance.`},{key:`B`,text:`They may be impractical to deploy.`},{key:`C`,text:`They may incur huge expenditure.`},{key:`D`,text:`They may be unwelcome to the public.`}],answer:`D`,explanation:`答案 D。根据题干核心词, 可定位到原文第三段。原文指出,she fears that tech’s inequality problem could be a road block to deploying AI. These are transformative technologies that change the ways we spend our time every day, that change business models that succeed ,这表明transformative technologies 给我们带来的巨大变化。第四段又随即指出, resentment is simmering among many as the benefits are perceived too to elites in a handful of prosperous cities.“resentment” 和“among many”可知,公众对此不买账。因此选项D符合题意。`,evidence:{paragraphId:`p1-2`,quote:`Improving living standards and increasing prosperity for more people will require greater use of digital technologies to boost productivity in various sectors, including health care and construction,…`},score:2},{id:`kaoyan2-2024-real-r24`,number:24,type:`single`,stem:`Several American cities are mentioned to show ___.`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`the uneven distribution of AI technologies in the US`},{key:`B`,text:`the disappointing prospect of tech jobs in the US`},{key:`C`,text:`the fast progress of US regional economies`},{key:`D`,text:`the increasing significance of US AI assets`}],answer:`A`,explanation:`答案 A。根据题干关键词 cities 可以定位到原文第五段。原文指出, a short list of eight American cities that ... had roughly 38% of all tech jobs by 2019. New AI Technologies are particularly concentrated:...estimate that just 15 cities account for two -thirds of the AI assets and capabilities in the United States. 通过数据分析可以发现, 在2019年8个城市拥有所有技术工作的38%, 而后又得知: 15合格城市占据2/3的人工智能资产和产能。美国有50个州,由此可知选项A符合题意。`,evidence:{paragraphId:`p1-5`,quote:`According to the Brookings Institution, a short list of eight American cities that included San Francisco, San Jose, Boston, and Seattle had roughly 38% of all tech jobs by 2019.`},score:2},{id:`kaoyan2-2024-real-r25`,number:25,type:`single`,stem:`With regard to Coyle's concern, the author suggests ___.`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`raising funds to start new AI projects`},{key:`B`,text:`encouraging collaboration in AI research`},{key:`C`,text:`guarding against the side effects of AI`},{key:`D`,text:`redefining the role of AI technologies`}],answer:`D`,explanation:`答案 D。原文第六段指出,Part of the solution could lie in somehow loosening the strangle hold that Big Tech has on defining the Al agenda. 第七段建议:A more immediate response is to broaden our digital imaginations lo conceive of Al technologies that don't simply replace jobs but expand opportunities in the sectors that different arts. 由此可以得知需要重新定位人工智能。所以选项D符合题意。`,evidence:{paragraphId:`p1-6`,quote:`Not only will this foster political and social unrest, but it could, as Coyle suggests, hold back the sorts of AI technologies needed for regional economies to grow.`},score:2},{id:`kaoyan2-2024-real-r26`,number:26,type:`single`,stem:`It can be learned from Paragraph 1 that the UK needs to ___.`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`increase its domestic wood supply`},{key:`B`,text:`reduce its demand for timber`},{key:`C`,text:`lower its wood production costs`},{key:`D`,text:`lift its control on timber imports`}],answer:`A`,explanation:`答案 A。原文开篇指出, 英国所面建筑危机的原因, 即 failure to plant trees to produce wood;随后指出 called for urgent action to reduce the country’s reliance on timber imports and provide a stable supply of wood for future generations. 下文还就木材需求国产和进口的数量分对比。由此可知选项A符合题意。`,evidence:{paragraphId:`p2-1`,quote:`The forestry and wood trade body has called for urgent action to reduce the country's reliance on timber imports and provide a stable supply of wood for future generations.`},score:2},{id:`kaoyan2-2024-real-r27`,number:27,type:`single`,stem:`According to Confor, the UK government's fresh incentives ___.`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`can hardly address a construction crisis`},{key:`B`,text:`are believed to come at a wrong time`},{key:`C`,text:`seem to be misleading for landowners`},{key:`D`,text:`will be too costly to put into practice`}],answer:`A`,explanation:`答案 A。根据题干关键词fresh incentives and Confor 定位到第二段。原文指出,Not only are we facing a carbon crisis now, but we will also be facing a future construction crisis because of a failure to plant trees to produce wood. 由此可知选项A符合题意。此外,该段上文贸易实体机构也指出,these (fresh incentives) don't go far enough and fail to promote the benefits of planting them to boost timber supplies.`,evidence:{paragraphId:`p2-1`,quote:`The UK is facing a future construction crisis because of a failure to plant trees to produce wood, Confor has warned.`},score:2},{id:`kaoyan2-2024-real-r28`,number:28,type:`single`,stem:`The UK's exposure to fluctuating wood prices is a result of ___.`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`the government's inaction on timber imports`},{key:`B`,text:`inadequate investment in growing wood`},{key:`C`,text:`the competition among timber traders at home`},{key:`D`,text:`wood producers' motive to maximise profits`}],answer:`B`,explanation:`答案 B。根据题干定位到原文第二段最后一句。该句指出: For decades we have not taken responsibility for investing in our domestic wood supply, leaving us exposed to fluctuating prices and fighting for future supplies of wood as global demand rises and our own supplies fall. 分析句子结构可知,leaving us... 作为伴随状态,表示主干句的行为结果。由此得知上文必有原因, 对照选项, 可以确定B为正确答案。`,evidence:{paragraphId:`p2-2`,quote:`“For decades we have not taken responsibility for investing in our domestic wood supply, leaving us exposed to fluctuating prices and fighting for future supplies of wood as global demand rises and…`},score:2},{id:`kaoyan2-2024-real-r29`,number:29,type:`single`,stem:`Which of the following causes the shortage of wood supply in the UK?`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`Excessive timber consumption in construction.`},{key:`B`,text:`Unfavourable conditions for growing wood.`},{key:`C`,text:`Outdated technologies of the wood industry.`},{key:`D`,text:`Farmers' unwillingness to plant trees.`}],answer:`D`,explanation:`答案 D。原文最后一段指出,While the UK government has stated its ambition for more tree planting, there has been little action on the ground.其中 there has been little action on the ground,就表明“实际上没有行动”,因此对照选项可知 D 为正确答案。`,evidence:{paragraphId:`p2-1`,quote:`The UK is facing a future construction crisis because of a failure to plant trees to produce wood, Confor has warned.`},score:2},{id:`kaoyan2-2024-real-r30`,number:30,type:`single`,stem:`What does Goodall think the UK government should do?`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`Subsidise the building of low-carbon homes.`},{key:`B`,text:`Pay greater attention to boosting rural economies.`},{key:`C`,text:`Provide more support for productive tree planting.`},{key:`D`,text:`Give priority to pursuing its net-zero strategy.`}],answer:`C`,explanation:`答案 C。原文最后一句指出 ,calling for much greater impetus behind those aspirations to ensure we have enough wood to meet increasing demand,则表明需要更大的推动力,由此可知选项C符合题意。`,evidence:{paragraphId:`p2-4`,quote:`While productive tree planting can deliver real financial benefits to rural economies and contribute to the UK's net-zero strategy, the focus of government support continues to be on food production…`},score:2},{id:`kaoyan2-2024-real-r31`,number:31,type:`single`,stem:`According to Paragraph 1, keeping unsafe aging drivers off the road ___.`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`is a new safety measure`},{key:`B`,text:`has become a disputed issue`},{key:`C`,text:`can be a tough task to complete`},{key:`D`,text:`will be beneficial to their health`}],answer:`C`,explanation:`答案 C。原文开篇指出one big challenge.由此可知困难重重,所以选项C为正确答案。`,evidence:{paragraphId:`p3-1`,quote:`One of the biggest challenges in keeping unsafe aging drivers off the road is convincing them that it's time to turn over the keys.`},score:2},{id:`kaoyan2-2024-real-r32`,number:32,type:`single`,stem:`The American Medical Association's advice ___.`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`has won support from drivers`},{key:`B`,text:`is generally considered unrealistic`},{key:`C`,text:`is widely dismissed as unnecessary`},{key:`D`,text:`has met with different responses`}],answer:`D`,explanation:`答案 D。根据题干定位到原文第二段。原文指出,Some states require physicians to report others allow but do not mandate reports, while a few consider a report breach of confidentiality 由此可知大家的反应不仅相同,所以选项D为正确答案。`,evidence:{paragraphId:`p3-2`,quote:`“The American Medical Association advises physicians that ‘in situations where clear evidence of substantial driving impairment implies a strong threat to patient and public safety, and where the…`},score:2},{id:`kaoyan2-2024-real-r33`,number:33,type:`single`,stem:`According to Dugan, efforts to keep older drivers safe ___.`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`have brought about big changes`},{key:`B`,text:`need to be well coordinated`},{key:`C`,text:`have gained public recognition`},{key:`D`,text:`call for relevant legal support`}],answer:`B`,explanation:`答案 B。原文第三段指出了问题,Part of the problem in keeping older drivers safe is that the difficulties are addressed piece meal by different professions with different focuses, including gerontologists, highway administration officials automotive engineers and other.这表明问题没有统一协调处理,而是被零散解决,而且各种专业人士如老年学家、公路管理官员和汽车工程师等各自关注的重点不同。这从侧面反应需要协调解决。所以选项B正确。`,evidence:{paragraphId:`p3-3`,quote:`Part of the problem in keeping older drivers safe is that the difficulties are addressed piecemeal by different professions with different focuses, including gerontologists, highway administration…`},score:2},{id:`kaoyan2-2024-real-r34`,number:34,type:`single`,stem:`Some older drivers have trouble driving because they tend to ___.`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`stick with bad driving habits`},{key:`B`,text:`have a weakened memory`},{key:`C`,text:`suffer from chronic pains`},{key:`D`,text:`neglect car maintenance`}],answer:`B`,explanation:`答案 B。由原文 patients who have trouble driving because they can't turn their heads or remember where they are going -or have gotten shorter and haven't changed their seat settings sufficiently to reach car pedals easily,由此可知选项B为正确答案。`,evidence:{paragraphId:`p3-3`,quote:`Part of the problem in keeping older drivers safe is that the difficulties are addressed piecemeal by different professions with different focuses, including gerontologists, highway administration…`},score:2},{id:`kaoyan2-2024-real-r35`,number:35,type:`single`,stem:`Dugan thinks that the solution to the problems of crashes may lie in ___.`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`upgrading self-driving vehicles`},{key:`B`,text:`developing senior-friendly cars`},{key:`C`,text:`renovating transport facilities`},{key:`D`,text:`adjusting the age limit for drivers`}],answer:`B`,explanation:`答案 B。原文最后一段指出:we need to do more to improve safety , 而且Dugan认为we need cars that a 90-year-old can drive comfortably. 这是对车提出了要求。Comfortably对应选项friendly,而senior对应 90-year-old,所以选项B正确。`,evidence:{paragraphId:`p3-6`,quote:`As long as there are other cars on the roads, self-driving cars won't solve the problems of crashes, said Dugan.`},score:2},{id:`kaoyan2-2024-real-r36`,number:36,type:`single`,stem:`The research findings are cited in Paragraph 1 to show ___.`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`the prevalence of health apps`},{key:`B`,text:`the public concern over health`},{key:`C`,text:`the popularity of smartphones`},{key:`D`,text:`the advancement of technology`}],answer:`A`,explanation:`答案 A。由原文最后一句指出,350,000 health apps were available on the market,90,000 of which launched in 2020 alone. 由此可知可用的健康APP很多,而且但就2020年就有9万个。这说明非常流行。因此选项A符合题意。`,evidence:{paragraphId:`p4-1`,quote:`Recent research found that 350,000 health apps were available on the market, 90,000 of which launched in 2020 alone.`},score:2},{id:`kaoyan2-2024-real-r37`,number:37,type:`single`,stem:`What does the author imply about existing health privacy law?`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`Its coverage needs to be extended.`},{key:`B`,text:`Its enforcement needs strengthening.`},{key:`C`,text:`It has discouraged medical misconduct.`},{key:`D`,text:`It has disappointed insurance companies.`}],answer:`A`,explanation:`答案 A。由题干关键词 existing health privacy law 定位到第二段。原文指出, Existing health privacy law, such ...Act, is primarily focused on the way hospitals, doctors offices. clinics and insurance companies store health records online,这表明现有的健康隐私法律主要焦聚在医院 ,医生办公室等地方。但下文又指出 The health information ... does not receive the same legal protections,表明没有得到同样的法律保护。由此可知,选项A符合题意。`,evidence:{paragraphId:`p4-2`,quote:`Existing health privacy law is primarily focused on the way hospitals, doctors' offices, clinics and insurance companies store health records online.`},score:2},{id:`kaoyan2-2024-real-r38`,number:38,type:`single`,stem:`Before sharing its users' health information, Flo Health is required to ___.`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`seek the approval of the FTC`},{key:`B`,text:`find qualified third parties`},{key:`C`,text:`remove irrelevant personal data`},{key:`D`,text:`obtain their explicit permission`}],answer:`D`,explanation:`答案 D。原文第二段指出, requiring the company to get app users' express affirmative consent before haring their health information as well as to instruct the third parties to delete the data they had obtained., 由此可知选项D为正确答案。`,evidence:{paragraphId:`p4-3`,quote:`The FTC alleged in a complaint that “despite express privacy claims, the company took control of users' sensitive fertility data and shared it with third parties.” Flo Health and the FTC settled the…`},score:2},{id:`kaoyan2-2024-real-r39`,number:39,type:`single`,stem:`What challenge is the FTC currently faced with?`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`The complexity of health information.`},{key:`B`,text:`The rapid increase in new health apps.`},{key:`C`,text:`The subtle deceptiveness of health apps.`},{key:`D`,text:`The difficulty in assessing consumer harm.`}],answer:`B`,explanation:`答案 B。原文第二段最后指出,the rate at which these health apps are hitting the market demonstrates just how immense of a challenge this is, 这表明健康应用程序迅速涌入市场的速度是FTC面临的巨大挑战。所以选项B符合题意。`,evidence:{paragraphId:`p4-4`,quote:`While the FTC is doing what it can to ensure apps are keeping their promises to consumers around the handling of their sensitive health information, the rate at which these health apps are hitting…`},score:2},{id:`kaoyan2-2024-real-r40`,number:40,type:`single`,stem:`It can be learned from the last paragraph that health data protection ___.`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`has been embraced by health app developers`},{key:`B`,text:`has been a focus of federal policy-making`},{key:`C`,text:`has encountered opposition in California`},{key:`D`,text:`has gained legislative support in some states`}],answer:`D`,explanation:`答案 D。原文最后一段开始说 “comprehensive federal privacy legislation seems unlikely in the short term“ ,这表明短期内实施不太现实, 但下文随即指出了其他州采取的措施。所以选项D符合题意。`,evidence:{paragraphId:`p4-5`,quote:`States have begun implementing their own solutions to shore up protections for consumer-generated health data.`},score:2}]},{id:`newtype`,kind:`reading`,title:`Section II  Reading Comprehension  Part B`,instructions:`Directions: Read the following text and match each of the numbered items in the left column to its corresponding information in the right column. There are two extra choices in the right column. Mark your answers on the ANSWER SHEET. (10 points)`,minutes:15,passages:[{id:`p1`,title:`Text`,paragraphs:[{id:`p1-1`,marker:`1`,text:`High school students eager to stand out in the college application process often participate in a litany of extracurricular activities hoping to bolster their chances of admission to a selective undergraduate institution. However, college admissions experts say that the quality of a college hopeful’s extracurricular activities matters more than the number of activities he or she participates in. Sue Rexford, the director of college guidance at the Charles E. Smith Jewish Day School, says it is not necessary for a student filling out the Common Application to list 10 activities in the application. “No college will expect that a student has a huge laundry list of extracurriculars that they have been passionately involved in each for an extended period of time,” Rexford wrote in an email. Experts say it is tougher to distinguish oneself in a school-affiliated extracurricular activity that is common among high school students than it is to stand out while doing an uncommon activity. “The competition to stand out and make an impact is going to be much stiffer, and so if they’re going to do a popular activity, I’d say, be the best at it,” says Sara Harberson, a college admissions consultant. High school students who have an impressive personal project they are working on independently often impress colleges, experts say. “For example, a student with an interest in entrepreneurship could demonstrate skill and potential by starting a profitable small business,” Olivia Valdes, the founder of Zen Admissions consulting firm, wrote in an email. Joseph Adegboyega-Edun, a Maryland high school guidance counselor, says unconventional extracurricular activities can help students impress college admissions offices, assuming they demonstrated serious commitment. “Again, since one of the big questions high school seniors must consider is ‘What makes you unique?,’ having an uncommon extracurricular activity vs. a conventional one is an advantage,” he wrote in an email. Experts say demonstrating talent in at least one extracurricular activity can help in the college admissions process, especially at top-tier undergraduate institutions. “Distinguishing yourself in one focused type of extracurricular activity can be a positive in the admissions process, especially for highly selective institutions, where having top grades and test scores is not enough,” Katie Kelley, admissions counselor at IvyWise admissions consultancy, wrote in an email. “Students need to have that quality or hook that will appeal to admissions officers and allow them to visualize how the student might come and enrich their campus community.” Extracurricular activities related to the college major declared on a college application are beneficial, experts suggest. “If you already know your major, having an extracurricular that fits into that major can be a big plus,” says Mayghin Levine, the manager of educational opportunities with The Cabbage Patch Settlement House, a Louisville, Kentucky, nonprofit community center. High school students who have had a strong positive influence on their community through an extracurricular activity may impress a college and win a scholarship, says Erica Gwyn, a former math and science magnet program assistant at a public high school who is now executive director of the Kaleidoscope Careers Academy in Atlanta, a nonprofit organization.`}]}],questions:[{id:`kaoyan2-2024-real-n41`,number:41,type:`single`,stem:`Sue Rexford`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`Students who stand out in a specific extracurricular activity will be favored by top-tier institutions.`},{key:`B`,text:`Students whose extracurricular activity has benefited their community are likely to win a scholarship.`},{key:`C`,text:`Undertaking too many extracurricular activities will hardly be seen as a plus by colleges.`},{key:`D`,text:`A student who exhibits abilities in doing business can impress colleges.`},{key:`E`,text:`High school students participating in a popular activity should excel in it.`},{key:`F`,text:`Engaging in uncommon activities can demonstrate students' determination and dedication.`},{key:`G`,text:`It is advisable for students to choose an extracurricular activity that is related to their future study at college.`}],answer:`C`,explanation:`答案 C。Sue Rexford 出现在文章的第3段和第4段,文章 has a huge laundry list of extracurricular activities 与选项 Undertaking too many extracurricular activities 对应; No college will expect that 与选项 will hardly be seen as a plus by colleges 对应,故C项正确。`,score:2},{id:`kaoyan2-2024-real-n42`,number:42,type:`single`,stem:`Sara Harberson`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`Students who stand out in a specific extracurricular activity will be favored by top-tier institutions.`},{key:`B`,text:`Students whose extracurricular activity has benefited their community are likely to win a scholarship.`},{key:`C`,text:`Undertaking too many extracurricular activities will hardly be seen as a plus by colleges.`},{key:`D`,text:`A student who exhibits abilities in doing business can impress colleges.`},{key:`E`,text:`High school students participating in a popular activity should excel in it.`},{key:`F`,text:`Engaging in uncommon activities can demonstrate students' determination and dedication.`},{key:`G`,text:`It is advisable for students to choose an extracurricular activity that is related to their future study at college.`}],answer:`E`,explanation:`答案 E。Sara Harbenson 出现在文章第 6段,文章 they与选项 High school students对应;文章be the best at it 与选项should excel in it 对应;文章 do a popular activity与选项participating in a popular activity 对应。可知E为正确答案。`,score:2},{id:`kaoyan2-2024-real-n43`,number:43,type:`single`,stem:`Katie Kelley`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`Students who stand out in a specific extracurricular activity will be favored by top-tier institutions.`},{key:`B`,text:`Students whose extracurricular activity has benefited their community are likely to win a scholarship.`},{key:`C`,text:`Undertaking too many extracurricular activities will hardly be seen as a plus by colleges.`},{key:`D`,text:`A student who exhibits abilities in doing business can impress colleges.`},{key:`E`,text:`High school students participating in a popular activity should excel in it.`},{key:`F`,text:`Engaging in uncommon activities can demonstrate students' determination and dedication.`},{key:`G`,text:`It is advisable for students to choose an extracurricular activity that is related to their future study at college.`}],answer:`A`,explanation:`答案 A。Katie Kalley 出现在文章的第 11段,文章 Distinguishing yourself in one focused type of extracurricular activity 与选项 Students who stands out in a specific extracurricular activity 对应;文章 can be a positive in the admissions process, especially for highly selective institutions 与选项 will be favored by top -tier institutions 对应。故A项正确。`,score:2},{id:`kaoyan2-2024-real-n44`,number:44,type:`single`,stem:`Mayghin Levine`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`Students who stand out in a specific extracurricular activity will be favored by top-tier institutions.`},{key:`B`,text:`Students whose extracurricular activity has benefited their community are likely to win a scholarship.`},{key:`C`,text:`Undertaking too many extracurricular activities will hardly be seen as a plus by colleges.`},{key:`D`,text:`A student who exhibits abilities in doing business can impress colleges.`},{key:`E`,text:`High school students participating in a popular activity should excel in it.`},{key:`F`,text:`Engaging in uncommon activities can demonstrate students' determination and dedication.`},{key:`G`,text:`It is advisable for students to choose an extracurricular activity that is related to their future study at college.`}],answer:`G`,explanation:`答案 G。Mayghin Leuine 出现在文章的倒数第二段 , 文章 Extracurricular activities related to the college major declared on a college application 与选项 an extracurricular activity that is related to their future study at college 以及 having an extracurricular that fits into that major 对应;文章 are beneficial 和 can be a big plus 与选项 It is advisable 对应。可以确定选项G为正确选项。`,score:2},{id:`kaoyan2-2024-real-n45`,number:45,type:`single`,stem:`Erica Gwyn`,options:[{key:`A`,text:`Students who stand out in a specific extracurricular activity will be favored by top-tier institutions.`},{key:`B`,text:`Students whose extracurricular activity has benefited their community are likely to win a scholarship.`},{key:`C`,text:`Undertaking too many extracurricular activities will hardly be seen as a plus by colleges.`},{key:`D`,text:`A student who exhibits abilities in doing business can impress colleges.`},{key:`E`,text:`High school students participating in a popular activity should excel in it.`},{key:`F`,text:`Engaging in uncommon activities can demonstrate students' determination and dedication.`},{key:`G`,text:`It is advisable for students to choose an extracurricular activity that is related to their future study at college.`}],answer:`B`,explanation:`答案 B。Erica Gwyn 出现在文章的最后一段,文章 students 和 extracurricular activity 在选项中复现 ;文章 had a strong positive influence on their community 与选项 has benefited their community 对应 ; 文章 may win a scholarship 与选项 are likely to win a scholarship 对应。对应选项B符合题意。`,score:2}]},{id:`translation`,kind:`translation`,title:`Section III  Translation`,instructions:`Directions: Translate the following text into Chinese. Write your translation on the ANSWER SHEET. (15 points)`,minutes:25,questions:[{id:`kaoyan2-2024-real-t46`,number:46,type:`translation`,stem:`With the smell of coffee and fresh bread floating in the air, stalls bursting with colourful vegetables and tempting cheeses, and the buzz of friendly chats, farmers' markets are a feast for the senses. They also provide an opportunity to talk to the people responsible for growing or raising your food, support your local economy and pick up fresh seasonal produce - all at the same time. Farmers' markets are usually weekly or monthly events, most often with outdoor stalls, which allow farmers or producers to sell their food directly to customers. The size or regularity of markets can vary from season to season, depending on the area's agricultural calendar, and you're likely to find different produce on sale at different times of the year. By cutting out the middlemen, the farmers secure more profit for their produce. Shoppers also benefit from seeing exactly where - and to whom - their money is going.`,answer:`参考译文`,explanation:`参考译文：空气中飘着咖啡和新鲜面包的香气，摊位上摆满色彩鲜艳的蔬菜和诱人的奶酪，耳边传来友好交谈的嗡嗡声，农贸市场是一场感官盛宴。它们还让人们有机会与种植或养殖食物的人交谈，支持当地经济，并同时买到新鲜的时令农产品。农贸市场通常是每周或每月举行的活动，多数设有户外摊位，使农民或生产者能够直接向顾客出售食物。市场的规模或举办规律会随季节变化而变化，这取决于当地的农业日历；一年中不同时间，你很可能会看到不同的农产品在出售。通过省去中间商，农民能从自己的产品中获得更多利润。购物者也能清楚看到自己的钱究竟流向哪里、流向谁。`,score:15}],reference:{translation:`空气中飘着咖啡和新鲜面包的香气，摊位上摆满色彩鲜艳的蔬菜和诱人的奶酪，耳边传来友好交谈的嗡嗡声，农贸市场是一场感官盛宴。它们还让人们有机会与种植或养殖食物的人交谈，支持当地经济，并同时买到新鲜的时令农产品。农贸市场通常是每周或每月举行的活动，多数设有户外摊位，使农民或生产者能够直接向顾客出售食物。市场的规模或举办规律会随季节变化而变化，这取决于当地的农业日历；一年中不同时间，你很可能会看到不同的农产品在出售。通过省去中间商，农民能从自己的产品中获得更多利润。购物者也能清楚看到自己的钱究竟流向哪里、流向谁。`}},{id:`writing1`,kind:`writing`,title:`Section IV  Writing  Part A`,instructions:`Suppose you and Jack are going to do a survey on the protection of old houses in an ancient town. Write him an email to 1) put forward your plan, and 2) ask for his opinion. Write your answer in about 100 words on the ANSWER SHEET. Do not use your own name in your email; use “Li Ming” instead. (10 points)`,minutes:20,questions:[{id:`kaoyan2-2024-real-w47`,number:47,type:`writing`,stem:`Suppose you and Jack are going to do a survey on the protection of old houses in an ancient town. Write him an email to 1) put forward your plan, and 2) ask for his opinion. Write your answer in about 100 words on the ANSWER SHEET. Do not use your own name in your email; use “Li Ming” instead. (10 points)`,answer:`见参考范文`,explanation:`写作任务：给Jack写邮件，提出关于古镇老房子保护调研的计划，并征求他的意见。按 Directions 规定的字数与署名要求作答；语言要点与结构可参考下方「参考范文」。`,score:10}],reference:{essay:`Dear Jack, I'm writing to share my plan for our survey on the protection of old houses in our ancient town, and to hear what you think. I suggest we begin next Saturday. In the morning, I will interview elderly residents about the houses' history, while you photograph the buildings and record their present condition. In the afternoon, we can hand out questionnaires to visitors to collect wider opinions on preservation. Does this arrangement suit you? Please feel free to share any suggestions or changes you would prefer, and we can discuss the details before we start. Yours, Li Ming`}},{id:`writing2`,kind:`writing`,title:`Section IV  Writing  Part B`,instructions:`Write an essay based on the chart below. In your essay, you should 1) describe and interpret the chart, and 2) give your comments. Write your answer in about 150 words on the ANSWER SHEET. (15 points)`,minutes:30,questions:[{id:`kaoyan2-2024-real-w48`,number:48,type:`writing`,stem:`Write an essay based on the chart below. In your essay, you should 1) describe and interpret the chart, and 2) give your comments. Write your answer in about 150 words on the ANSWER SHEET. (15 points)`,answer:`见参考范文`,explanation:`写作任务：图表展示某高校劳动实践课程学生主要收获调查：学习了相关知识91.3%，提升了动手能力84.8%，感受到心情舒畅54.4%，增强了合作能力32.6%。按 Directions 规定的字数作答，围绕图表/图画描述、阐释与评论展开；参考范文见下方。`,score:15}],reference:{essay:`As is shown in the bar chart, a survey on students' main gains from a university's labor practice course lists four benefits. Learning relevant knowledge tops the list at 91.3%, closely followed by improved hands-on ability at 84.8%. Feeling relaxed accounts for 54.4%, while enhanced cooperation ranks lowest, at only 32.6%. Behind these figures lies a clear message. That knowledge and practical skills score so high suggests such courses effectively combine theory with practice, which is exactly their design purpose. The low figure for cooperation, however, may indicate that most tasks are completed individually, offering students few chances to work as a team. In my view, labor practice deserves greater emphasis in schools, for it cultivates abilities that textbooks alone cannot. Meanwhile, educators should redesign group-based tasks so that cooperation is strengthened. Only in this way can such courses truly benefit students in an all-round manner.`}}]}};export{e as default};